From 7bbd7919d8ac3b807952f64d7f0321e66e5a8eef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 22:19:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 76/78] hw/misc: the bench: analog co-simulation, wired Clicks,
 event recorder

Three links from a board's twin to the Peripheral Pretender bench, on
the PIC32CM boards and the PyKit (curiosity-circuitpython):

- pp-cosim (machine "cosim=<chardev>"): a circuit simulated outside
  QEMU, in lockstep. It sees every pad's electrical state (high, low,
  pulled, floating: mchp_port_observe(), mchp_port_pad_state()) and
  drives the input pads wired to it and the ADC inputs; the U2247 ADC
  reads an AIN the circuit drives at the end of its sampling phase.
- Wired Clicks (machine "wired=name=click:role.PAD:..."): a Click on any
  pads rather than a header. Its SPI and I2C reach every SERCOM that
  can serve those pads, while the pads are muxed to it (pp-bus-tap); its
  inputs listen to the pads beside the board's own parts
  (mchp_port_pad_listen()).
- pp-trace (machine "trace=<chardev>"): an event recorder. Pad levels
  (the PORT reports each change, pp_trace_pad()), SERCOM UART, SPI and
  I2C traffic, NVIC pend, entry and return (an observer hook in
  armv7m_nvic.c) and resets, stamped with QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL, as 16-byte
  records. It knows no device: the SoC glue registers the pad source
  and the interrupt observer, then attaches it. The reader schedules
  inputs ("at <t> <id> set <path> <prop> <value>", "at <t> <id>
  reset"), applied on a virtual timer in the order they came and
  reported with the instant each took effect, and paces a deterministic
  run (-icount shift=4,sleep=off) to real time by pausing the VM.
- Injected faults and input: PORT "pX-short" (pads shorted to VDD or
  GND over every driver), SERCOM "fault-nack" (I2C addresses that
  NACK), "fault-miso" (what the SPI host reads) and "rx-inject"
  (characters into the receiver, at a time the recorder knows).

qtest pic32cm-click-test: the faults and rx-inject.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
